# The Keys panel, opened with Down four times and Enter, with ESC O B and
# j among them: the key table.
size: 160x50
keys: \eOB\e[Bj
keys: j\r
screen:
| microL4 terminal demo                                                                                                                                   160x50 |
|                                                                                                                                                                |
| ╭─ Menu ───────────────╮ ╔═ Keys ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗ |
| │   1 Overview         │ ║                                                                                                                                   ║ |
| │   2 Attributes       │ ║ Bytes                  Key     Effect                                                                                             ║ |
| │   3 Colours          │ ║ ESC [ A, ESC O A, k    Up      the selection moves up, stopping at item 1                                                         ║ |
| │   4 Boxes            │ ║ ESC [ B, ESC O B, j    Down    the selection moves down, stopping at item 6                                                       ║ |
| │ > 5 Keys             │ ║ CR, LF                 Enter   opens the selected panel; on Quit, quits                                                           ║ |
| │   6 Quit             │ ║ 1 to 6                         selects that item and opens it                                                                     ║ |
| ╰──────────────────────╯ ║ q                              quits                                                                                              ║ |
|                          ║ any other                      logged as an unknown key                                                                           ║ |
|                          ║                                                                                                                                   ║ |
|                          ║ Keys reach tui through console, where client 4 is raw: Ctrl-T 4 gives                                                             ║ |
|                          ║ them to term, Ctrl-T Ctrl-T sends one Ctrl-T, and Ctrl-T 1 gives them                                                             ║ |
|                          ║ back to root. term passes them on as typed, VT sequences and all.                                                                 ║ |
